@startuml
title Windows recording hotkey and tray ownership

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
left to right direction

actor User
component "Win32 owner thread\ntray HWND + message pump" as UI
component "Recording shortcut controller\nregistration + suspension set" as Shortcut
component "Recording controller\nsingle projected state" as Recording
component "Microphone capture service\ncues + WASAPI + private draft" as Capture
component "Window / tray projection\nEN/RU text + explicit fallback" as Projection

User --> UI : hotkey / button / tray / Esc
UI --> Shortcut : start, reconfigure, lock,\nsuspend, resume, quit
Shortcut --> UI : WM_HOTKEY registration id
UI --> Recording : toggle / cancel / lifecycle stop
Recording --> Capture : async start / stop(reason)
Capture --> Recording : terminal outcome
Recording --> Projection : idle / processing / active / failed
Shortcut --> Projection : registered / conflict /\nunavailable / suspended

note bottom of UI
RegisterHotKey and UnregisterHotKey run only here.
Esc is a foreground-window accelerator, never a global hook.
Hidden recording exposes an explicit tray Cancel command.
end note

note bottom of Recording
Win32 callbacks only enqueue bounded controller work.
Shutdown drains capture after the message pump exits.
end note

@enduml
